kwin 6.7.5: make the screenshot target's OpenGL context current before painting

Backport of the upstream fix for the kwin_wayland crash that happens whenever a
QML based effect (e.g. showfps) is loaded and any ScreenShot2, Spectacle or
xdg-desktop-portal capture is made.

WorkspaceScene::prePaint() calls effects->prePaintScreen().  A QML effect that
paints an OffscreenQuickScene for the (new) ScreenShot render view constructs an
OffscreenQuickView there; its constructor makes its own QOpenGLContext current
and then calls doneCurrent(), which sets KWin's process wide
EglContext::s_currentContext to nullptr.  The screenshot path then painted into
the screenshot framebuffer without making a context current again, so
GLFramebuffer::pushFramebuffer() dereferenced the null current context and
kwin_wayland died with SIGSEGV in EglContext::currentFramebuffer().

Upstream fixed this in two steps that this patch backports:

  * ScreenshotLayer::doBeginFrame() now makes the target framebuffer's context
    current (GLFramebuffer::context() is the new accessor it needs), and
  * both SceneView based ScreenShotManager::takeScreenShot() overloads call
    layer.beginFrame() *after* sceneView.prePaint(), so that the makeCurrent()
    happens after the effects had their chance to switch the context.

The DRM backend never had this problem because EglGbmLayerSurface::startRendering()
already makes the compositor's context current before every composite.

diff --git a/src/opengl/glframebuffer.h b/src/opengl/glframebuffer.h
index 8651eb4..71a1f81 100644
--- a/src/opengl/glframebuffer.h
+++ b/src/opengl/glframebuffer.h
@@ -83,6 +83,14 @@ public:
         return m_valid;
     }
 
+    /**
+     * Returns the OpenGL context this framebuffer object belongs to.
+     */
+    EglContext *context() const
+    {
+        return m_context;
+    }
+
     /**
      * Returns the last bound framebuffer, or @c null if no framebuffer is current.
      */
